#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:3
msgid "Descriptions de robots avec ROS2"
msgstr "Robot Descriptions with ROS2"

#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:5
msgid ""
"Le but de la description d'un robot est d'avoir un modèle servant à la "
"fois à la simulation et au contrôle du robot:"
msgstr ""
"The purpose of a robot description is to have a model that serves both "
"simulation and control of the robot:"

#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:7
msgid "visualiser le robot et ses configurations géométriques,"
msgstr "visualize the robot and its geometric configurations,"

#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:8
msgid "calculer la position des segments du robot en fonction des articulations,"
msgstr "calculate the position of the robot's segments based on the joints,"

#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:9
msgid ""
"faire intéragir le robot dans un environnement de simulation et récupérer "
"des données capteurs, des données de collisions, des informations de "
"position, vitesse, accélération et force exercées (entre autre sur les "
"articulations et les segments du robot),"
msgstr ""
"interact with the robot in a simulation environment and retrieve sensor "
"data, collision data, position, velocity, acceleration, and force "
"information (among others on the joints and segments of the robot),"

#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:11
msgid ""
"Les descriptions de robots sont faites dans des fichiers de description "
"de robot. Nous utiliserons 2 formats XML dans ROS: URDF et SDF."
msgstr ""
"Robot descriptions are made in robot description files. We will use two "
"XML formats in ROS: URDF and SDF."

#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:14
msgid "Ces fichiers décrivent principalement les paramètres suivants:"
msgstr "These files mainly describe the following parameters:"

#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:16
msgid "les segments du robot:"
msgstr "the robot's segments:"

#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:18
msgid "pour la visualisaiton"
msgstr "for visualization"

#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:20
msgid "géometrie (:code:`<geometry>`),"
msgstr "geometry (:code:`<geometry>`),"

#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:21
#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:27
msgid ""
"origine (position et orientation d'un repère différent du repère "
"d'origine du segment)"
msgstr ""
"origin (position and orientation of a frame different from the segment's "
"origin frame)"

#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:22
msgid "matériel (principalement la couleur)"
msgstr "material (mainly color)"

#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:24
msgid "pour le calcul de collision"
msgstr "for collision calculation"

#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:26
msgid ""
"géometrie (:code:`<geometry>`) souvent une géométrie simplifiée pour "
"accélérer les calculs,"
msgstr ""
"geometry (:code:`<geometry>`), often simplified geometry to speed up "
"calculations,"

#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:29
msgid "paramètres d'inértie"
msgstr "inertia parameters"

#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:31
msgid "masse,"
msgstr "mass,"

#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:32
msgid ""
"`centre d'inertie <https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Centre_d%27inertie>`_ "
"(centre de gravité),"
msgstr ""
"`center of inertia <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Center_of_mass>`_ "
"(center of gravity),"

#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:33
msgid "`matrice d'inertie <https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moment_d%27inertie>`_"
msgstr ""
"`inertia matrix <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moment_of_inertia>`_"

#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:35
msgid "les articulations entre les pairs de segments reliés,"
msgstr "the joints between connected pairs of segments,"

#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:37
msgid "nom"
msgstr "name"

#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:38
msgid "type (prismatique, pivot d'axe, rigide, etc.)"
msgstr "type (prismatic, revolute, fixed, etc.)"

#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:39
msgid "parent et enfant (les 2 segments reliés)"
msgstr "parent and child (the two connected segments)"

#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:40
msgid ""
"origine (la transformation entre les 2 segments avant qu'aucun mouvement "
"ne soit appliqué)"
msgstr ""
"origin (the transformation between the two segments before any movement "
"is applied)"

#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:41
msgid ""
"limites de mouvement (limites de position, vitesse, accélération, force, "
"etc.)"
msgstr ""
"motion limits (position, velocity, acceleration, force limits, etc.)"

#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:42
msgid "axe du mouvement"
msgstr "axis of motion"

#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:46
msgid "Chaînes cinématiques"
msgstr "Kinematic Chains"

#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:48
msgid ""
"Le passage du repère d'un segment à un autre suite à la transformation "
"appliquée par l'articulation reliant les 2 segment constitue la "
"transformation cinématique élémentaire de la chaîne cinématique du robot."
msgstr ""
"The transition from the frame of one segment to another following the "
"transformation applied by the joint connecting the two segments "
"constitutes the elementary kinematic transformation of the robot's "
"kinematic chain."

#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:55
msgid ""
"Arbre des chaînes cinématiques des jambes du robot Hubo KHR-4, un robot "
"humanoïde non parallèle, (source: "
":cite:`Ali2010_closed_form_inverse_kinematic_joint_solution_for_humanoid_robots`"
" .)"
msgstr ""
"Kinematic chain tree of the legs of the Hubo KHR-4 robot, a non-parallel "
"humanoid robot, (source: "
":cite:`Ali2010_closed_form_inverse_kinematic_joint_solution_for_humanoid_robots`"
" .)"

#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:57
msgid ""
"Le premier segment de la chaîne cinématique est appelé la racine de la "
"chaîne cinématique."
msgstr ""
"The first segment of the kinematic chain is called the root of the "
"kinematic chain."

#: ../../source/c01_robot_modeling/c01s02_robot_descriptions.rst:59
msgid ""
"La racine de la chaîne cinématique est un segment fixe par rapport au "
"repère de modélisation, souvent appelé repère monde (world en anglais). "
"Le sens des flêches indique quel est le repère de référence pour la "
"position et l'orientation du segment suivant. Dans les paramètres de "
"description ci-dessus, la flêche va de l'enfant vers le parent."
msgstr ""
"The root of the kinematic chain is a fixed segment relative to the "
"modeling frame, often called the world frame. The direction of the arrows "
"indicates which frame is the reference for the position and orientation "
"of the next segment. In the description parameters above, the arrow goes "
"from the child to the parent."